-- title:
--   Integral q-expansion quotients lie in the localised modular ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q \in A$ a nonunit (the hypothesis `LiesOverPrime`), let $N \ge 1$ be an integer with $q \nmid N$, and let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, that is, of the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise image of the field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the divisor expansions at level $Nq$. Assume there exist Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise image of $y$ under the residue map $A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ is nonzero and such that, after pushing $x$ and $y$ forward along the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, one has $f \cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$. Then $f$, viewed as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (N * q) A.toSubring (IsLocalRing.residue A)`: there are $r, s$ in the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$, with the coefficientwise reduction of $s$ nonzero, such that $f \cdot s = r$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Gauss-valuation integrality condition on the $\mathfrak q$-expansion of a level-$Nq$ modular function already forces membership in the modular ring $A[j, j_{Nq}]$ localised at the kernel of coefficientwise reduction, for a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ with $q \nmid N$. It supplies the nontrivial half of the dichotomy [`ModularCurve.coe_mem_modularLocalized_or_coe_inv_mem_modularLocalized_mul_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.coe_mem_modularLocalized_or_coe_inv_mem_modularLocalized_mul_of_not_dvd), by which this localised ring cuts out a valuation ring of the function field of $X_0(Nq)$.
